.TH HAMSTIK 1 "HAMSTIK WORK EDIT"
.SH NAME
hamstik work edit \- Edit a work item
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamstik work edit [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edit a work item
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I KEY
Work item key
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --title
New title
.TP
.B --description
New description text
.TP
.B --description-file
New description source (path, or - for stdin)
.TP
.B --description-editor
Author the description in $VISUAL/$EDITOR instead of passing text
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --type
New work item type
Choices: task, bug, story, feature, epic
.TP
.B --priority
New priority
Choices: low, medium, high, urgent
.TP
.B --assignee
New assignee (or `me`)
.TP
.B --sprint
Sprint id
.TP
.B --parent
New parent key (or parent UUID)
.TP
.B --story-points
New story point estimate
.TP
.B --due-date
New due date. Accepts RFC 3339, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `today`/`yesterday`/`tomorrow`, or a relative offset such as `7d`, `2w`, or `+3h`; input without a UTC offset is read in the host's local time zone
.TP
.B --attribute-option
Set a select option as ATTRIBUTE_KEY=OPTION_KEY (repeat the key for multi-select values)
.TP
.B --attribute-boolean
Set a boolean Attribute as ATTRIBUTE_KEY=true|false
.TP
.B --clear-attribute
Explicitly clear an existing Attribute assignment
.TP
.B --clear-description
Clear the description
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-assignee
Unassign the item
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-sprint
Remove the sprint
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-parent
Detach the parent
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-story-points
Clear the story point estimate
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --clear-due-date
Clear the due date
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --force
Bypass revision conflict protection (If-Match: *)
Choices: true, false
.TP
.B --idempotency-key
Explicit idempotency key (used for Attribute-bearing updates)
